{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-djokovic-exits-us-open-in-first-round", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Djokovic exits US Open in first round", "summary": "Novak Djokovic lost his US Open opener to Mariano Navone, his first ever first-round exit at Flushing Meadows, breaking down in tears.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/c39m1le9gjeo", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Novak Djokovic, the 24-time Grand Slam champion and fourth seed, lost his opening match to Argentina's Mariano Navone 7–6 (7–5) 5–7 4–6 6–2 6–1, breaking down in tears in the deciding set of a match in which he struggled physically throughout — he was seen vomiting into a courtside bin. It is the first time in 20 appearances that Djokovic has lost in the first round at the US Open (he had won all 19 previous openers), and his first opening-round defeat at any Grand Slam since 2006. The 39-year-old, chasing a record 25th major, congratulated the 25-year-old Navone on the biggest win of his career.", "why": "This is the clearest evidence yet that the last man standing from tennis's \"Big Three\" is being caught by time — and it landed the day after his greatest rival was formally enshrined in the sport's history.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-djokovic-exits-us-open-in-first-round", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Novak Djokovic", "Mariano Navone", "US Open"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-federer-inducted-into-tennis-hall-of-fame", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Federer inducted into Tennis Hall of Fame", "summary": "Swiss great Roger Federer was tearfully inducted into the International Tennis Hall of Fame at Newport.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/cvgy6zzgwlgo", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland's Roger Federer was inducted into the International Tennis Hall of Fame, calling it \"one of the greatest honours\" of his life. The 20-time Grand Slam singles champion, who retired in 2022, was tearful at the Newport ceremony in front of greats including Billie Jean King and John McEnroe. Federer won a record eight Wimbledon titles, six Australian Opens, five US Opens and one French Open, and spent 310 weeks as world number one — the mark later surpassed by Djokovic.", "why": "A Swiss sporting icon receives tennis's ultimate lifetime recognition — and the timing, one day before Djokovic's collapse in New York, underlined how completely one era is giving way to the next.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-federer-inducted-into-tennis-hall-of-fame", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Roger Federer", "International Tennis Hall of Fame"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-young-boys-and-basel-draw-3-3", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Young Boys and Basel draw 3-3", "summary": "Swiss Super League heavyweights Young Boys and Basel drew 3-3 in round five, leaving the title race congested.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The season's two heavyweights met at Bern's Wankdorf on Saturday and produced a six-goal stalemate: Young Boys 3–3 Basel, neither side able to land the decisive blow. That leaves Young Boys unbeaten but held, and hands the early initiative to the week's quieter stories — Lugano won 2–1 at Sion to stretch a winning run to four, while defending champions Thun (crowned for the first time in the club's history last season) rallied to win 4–3 away at St. Gallen, who lost for the first time. Promoted Vaduz thrashed Grasshoppers 5–2 for a maiden win of the campaign, Zürich won at Lausanne, and ten-man Luzern clung on for a 1–1 draw at Servette. Five rounds in, the title picture is congested rather than settled.", "why": "The two clubs most Swiss fans expect to contest the title spent 90 minutes proving how even the top of the table is — good news for a league that wants a race, not a procession.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-young-boys-and-basel-draw-3-3", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Young Boys", "FC Basel", "Swiss Super League", "Thun", "Lugano"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-fernandes-hat-trick-sparks-man-utd-comeback", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Fernandes hat-trick sparks Man Utd comeback", "summary": "Bruno Fernandes scored a hat-trick as Manchester United came from behind to beat Ipswich 5-2 as the transfer window neared its deadline.", "url": "https://www.premierleague.com/results", "source_domain": "premierleague.com", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Manchester United trailed Ipswich Town before Bruno Fernandes scored a hat-trick in a 5–2 comeback win — a marker of intent for Michael Carrick's rebuild, on a day when Marcus Rashford made his first Premier League start for the club since December 2024 and teenager Kobbie Mainoo returned to the side. Chelsea, meanwhile, kept a perfect start with a seven-goal thriller against Brighton. The bigger backdrop is the calendar: the summer transfer window shuts at the start of September, and the marquee confirmed departure is Ollie Watkins, Aston Villa's record Premier League scorer (91 goals), completing a £51m move to Al-Hilal of the Saudi Pro League on a three-year deal.", "why": "Two early-season statements from clubs with title ambitions — and a reminder that Saudi money is still strong enough to pull a 30-year-old England international out of the Premier League at his peak.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-fernandes-hat-trick-sparks-man-utd-comeback", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Manchester United", "Bruno Fernandes", "Michael Carrick", "Ollie Watkins", "Al-Hilal"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-fia-lifts-russia-ban-ukraine-complains", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "FIA lifts Russia ban, Ukraine complains", "summary": "The FIA lifted its ban on Russian and Belarusian competitors, prompting a formal ethics complaint from Ukraine's motorsport federation.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/general/news/ukraine-files-complaint-to-fia-ethics-committee-after-russian-ban-lift/10850119/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Motorsport's governing body, the FIA, has lifted the ban on Russian and Belarusian competitors in international events — a ban in place since Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine. The move, approved by the FIA's World Council and reportedly proposed by president Mohammed Ben Sulayem, drew an immediate formal complaint to the FIA ethics committee from the Ukrainian Automobile Federation (FAU), which is demanding an urgent investigation of its Russian counterpart. The FAU says the Russian federation operates offices in Russian-occupied parts of Ukraine — Crimea, Sevastopol, and the Donetsk and Zaporizhzhia regions, all UN-recognised as Ukrainian territory — in breach of FIA statutes that permit only one motoring club per country.", "why": "Sport keeps being asked to referee geopolitics. The FIA's decision would let Russian drivers back onto international grids while the war continues, and Ukraine is framing it as a governance breach rather than a sporting one.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-fia-lifts-russia-ban-ukraine-complains", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-27", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FIA", "Mohammed Ben Sulayem", "Ukraine", "Russia"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-norris-extends-mclaren-deal-to-2030", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Norris extends McLaren deal to 2030", "summary": "Reigning world champion Lando Norris signed a contract extension with McLaren running to the end of 2030.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/norris-extends-mclaren-deal-until-f1-2030/10850350/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Reigning world champion Lando Norris has signed a contract extension keeping him at McLaren through the end of 2030, committing the sport's current benchmark driver to the constructors' champions for the long term.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-norris-extends-mclaren-deal-to-2030", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lando Norris", "McLaren"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-pogacar-out-of-vuelta-mas-takes-red-jersey", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Pogacar out of Vuelta, Mas takes red jersey", "summary": "Race leader Tadej Pogacar abandoned the Vuelta after a stage-eight crash needing collarbone surgery; Enric Mas inherited the lead and won stage nine.", "url": "https://www.lavuelta.es/en/news/2026/stage-9/mas-proves-more-than-up-to-la-roja/59672", "source_domain": "lavuelta.es", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A week after the Vuelta a España — the third and final of cycling's three-week Grand Tours — opened with Tadej Pogačar in command, the world champion is out. Pogačar, the overwhelming favourite chasing the one Grand Tour missing from his career, crashed with about 33km left of Saturday's eighth stage and abandoned the race; his UAE Team Emirates doctor reported a broken left collarbone requiring surgery (delayed for concussion precautions), a concussion and a \"stable\" neck fracture. It is the first Grand Tour he has ever failed to finish. He had led by 3 minutes 50 seconds. Spain's Enric Mas inherited the leader's red jersey — declining to wear it on Saturday's podium out of respect — and then won Sunday's ninth stage atop the Aitana climb, extending his overall lead (the general classification, i.e. cumulative time) to 1:18 over Primož Roglič, with Félix Gall third and Britain's Oscar Onley up to fourth.", "why": "The most dominant stage racer of his generation was removed from a race he was strangling — and a Grand Tour that looked finished is suddenly a genuine contest with two weeks still to ride.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-pogacar-out-of-vuelta-mas-takes-red-jersey", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Tadej Pogacar", "Enric Mas", "Vuelta a Espana", "Primoz Roglic", "Oscar Onley"]}
{"id": "2026-08-31-sports-werro-nears-oldest-world-record-in-zurich", "date": "2026-08-31", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Werro nears oldest world record in Zurich", "summary": "Swiss runner Audrey Werro clocked the third-fastest 800m in history at Weltklasse Zurich, closing on athletics' oldest outdoor world record.", "url": "https://weltklassezuerich.ch/en/news/", "source_domain": "weltklassezuerich.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "On a record-breaking night at the Zurich Diamond League (the elite one-day meeting series), Swiss European champion Audrey Werro ran 1:53.70 over 800m — the third-fastest time in history — finishing just 0.42 seconds shy of Jarmila Kratochvilová's 1:53.28, set in 1983 and the oldest outdoor world record in athletics. Roared on by a 25,000-strong home crowd, the 22-year-old set a personal best and now holds four of the ten fastest 800m times ever run, all recorded this summer. She was not alone in threatening the history books: the same meeting produced two world records — Alison dos Santos in the 400m hurdles and Russell in the 100m hurdles.", "why": "A 43-year-old record that has outlasted whole eras of the sport now looks beatable, and a Swiss athlete on home soil is the one making it look inevitable — \"sooner rather than later,\" in her own read of the race.", "thread_id": "2026-08-31-sports-werro-nears-oldest-world-record-in-zurich", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-31", "event_date": "2026-08-27", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Audrey Werro", "Weltklasse Zurich", "Jarmila Kratochvilova", "Alison dos Santos"]}
